  <main id="main">

    <section class="page-head industry-head ia-head">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="ia-connected" id="connected" data-connected hidden role="status"></div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Inbox Assistant</span>
        <h1>Every routine customer email, drafted in seconds. <em>Your team just checks and sends.</em></h1>
        <p class="lead hero__say">Paste in a customer email and it writes the reply in seconds, from your own prices and policies, on a private page made for your business. Anything it can&rsquo;t be sure of is marked for a person to fill in. <b>Nothing goes out without someone pressing send.</b></p>
        <ul class="ia-facts" aria-label="At a glance">
          <li><b><span data-zar="9500">R9,500</span></b><span>setup, paid only once it works</span></li>
          <li><b><span data-zar="2950">R2,950</span></b><span>a month once you keep it, AI usage included</span></li>
          <li><b>3 business days</b><span>at most, to your own page</span></li>
          <li><b>Pay nothing</b><span>until it saves you 5 hours a week</span></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="btn-row page-head__cta">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--large" href="https://calendar.app.google/58FYamh1ahXB4khM9" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track="cta-inbox-book-top">Book a free 30-minute call</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--large" href="#try" data-track="cta-inbox-try" data-needs-ai>Try it on one of your emails</a><a class="btn btn--ghost btn--large" href="live-demo?sample=email" data-track="cta-inbox-watch" data-ai-off>Watch it work on an inbox</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="callwhat" aria-label="What happens on the free call"><li>You tell us about the work</li><li>We say honestly if AI fits</li><li>No slides, no pitch</li><li>You leave with a rough price, or an honest &ldquo;not worth it&rdquo;</li></ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- the guarantee and who it's for -->
    <section class="section" id="guarantee" aria-labelledby="guarTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="ia-guarantee reveal">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">You pay last</span>
            <h2 id="guarTitle">We set it up for you first. You pay only once it&rsquo;s saving your team 5 hours a week.</h2>
            <p>On day one we time how long your team spends on customer email now, and agree how we&rsquo;ll measure it. Then we set up your private page, and your team uses it on real customer emails for two weeks at no cost. After each reply they tap how it went (sent as is, sent after edits, or not used), so the time saved is measured the same way every time. If it&rsquo;s saving at least 5 hours a week, you pay the setup and the monthly plan starts. If it isn&rsquo;t, you pay nothing and we switch it off.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ia-fit">
            <h3>Who it&rsquo;s for</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><b>20 or more customer emails a day</b>: quotes, bookings, orders, &ldquo;where&rsquo;s my&hellip;&rdquo;, the same questions</li>
              <li><b>Any email system</b>: Gmail, Outlook or anything else you can copy an email from</li>
              <li><b>Prices and policies you can share with us</b>, even if they&rsquo;re in a spreadsheet or someone&rsquo;s head</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="small muted">Fewer emails than that? We&rsquo;ll tell you on the call that it probably isn&rsquo;t worth it yet, and suggest something simpler.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- before you hire -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="hire" aria-labelledby="hireTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Before you hire</span>
          <h2 id="hireTitle">Thinking of hiring someone for the inbox? Try this first.</h2>
          <p>It doesn&rsquo;t replace a good person. It takes the typing off the people you have, so they can do the work that needs them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ia-compare reveal">
          <div class="ia-col">
            <h3>A new admin hire</h3>
            <p class="ia-price">about <span data-zar="15000">R15,000</span> to <span data-zar="25000">R25,000</span> <small>a month</small></p>
            <ul><li>Weeks to recruit and train</li><li>Office hours, leave and sick days</li><li>Still types every reply by hand</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="ia-col ia-col--us">
            <h3>Inbox Assistant</h3>
            <p class="ia-price"><span data-zar="2950">R2,950</span> <small>a month, plus <span data-zar="9500">R9,500</span> setup</small></p>
            <ul><li>Ready within 3 business days, nothing to pay until it works</li><li>Drafts ready day and night, also over weekends</li><li>Your team checks and sends in seconds</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- the timeline: promised at 3 business days, aimed at 1 -->
    <section class="section" id="how" aria-labelledby="howTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
          <h2 id="howTitle">Ready within 3 business days. About an hour of your time.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps steps--tight reveal">
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">1</span><h3>Day 1: a one-hour call</h3><p>We look at your emails together, time how long they take now, and agree the target.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">2</span><h3>We set it up</h3><p>Your own private page, loaded with your prices, policies and the way you like to reply.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">3</span><h3>You test it</h3><p>Your team tries it on real emails. We fix anything that reads wrong.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">4</span><h3>Two weeks on real emails, then you decide</h3><p>Paste an email, get the reply, tap how it went. We add up the time saved, and you pay only if it hits the target.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- try it -->
    <section class="section section--tint aid-sec" id="try" data-needs-ai aria-labelledby="tryTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="aid-head reveal">
          <div><span class="eyebrow">See it first</span><h2 id="tryTitle">Paste one of your own customer emails. See the reply it would draft.</h2></div>
          <dl class="aid-psr"><dt>Note</dt><dd>This version doesn&rsquo;t know your prices or dates yet, so it leaves gaps for you to fill. Set up for you, it fills them from your own information.</dd></dl>
        </div>
        <div class="aid try reveal" data-try>
          <div class="aid__bar"><span class="aid__tag aid__tag--live">Live AI</span><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost btn--small" data-try-sample>Use a sample email</button></div>
          <form class="form try__form" data-try-form novalidate>
            <div class="form-row">
              <label for="tryEmail">A customer email</label>
              <textarea id="tryEmail" name="email" rows="7" maxlength="3000" required placeholder="Paste an email a customer sent you"></textarea>
              <p class="form__hint">Take out names, phone numbers and account details first. We don&rsquo;t keep what you paste.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="form-row">
              <label for="tryBiz">What does your business do? <span class="optional">optional</span></label>
              <input id="tryBiz" name="business" type="text" maxlength="200" autocomplete="off" placeholder="e.g. Aircon installs and servicing in Pretoria" />
            </div>
            <div class="try__go"><button type="submit" class="btn btn--primary">Draft the reply</button><p class="small muted try__msg" data-try-msg aria-live="polite"></p></div>
          </form>
          <div class="try__out" data-try-out hidden>
            <p class="try__gist"><b>What they want:</b> <span data-try-gist></span></p>
            <div class="try__reply"><h4>The draft reply <small>ready for you</small></h4><div class="try__text" data-try-reply></div></div>
            <div class="try__check" data-try-checkbox><h4>You check before sending</h4><ul data-try-check></ul></div>
            <div class="try__acts"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost btn--small" data-try-copy>Copy the reply</button><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost btn--small" data-try-again>Try another email</button></div>
            <p class="try__next">Want this on every email, with your prices and policies filled in? <a class="inline-link" href="https://calendar.app.google/58FYamh1ahXB4khM9" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track="cta-inbox-try-book">Book a free 30-minute call</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- founding clients (shown only while the offer runs) -->
    <section class="section founding" id="founding" aria-labelledby="foundTitle" data-founding hidden>
      <div class="container">
        <div class="founding__card">
          <span class="offer-note__tag">Founding clients</span>
          <h2 id="foundTitle">We&rsquo;re new. We&rsquo;d rather prove it than claim it.</h2>
          <p class="founding__lead">Our first <span data-f-total>5</span> clients who keep it get the Inbox Assistant setup <b data-f-offword>free</b>: <b data-f-price>R0</b> instead of <s data-f-was>R9,500</s>.</p>
          <ul class="founding__list">
            <li><b>What you get.</b> The setup <span data-f-offword2>free</span>, even when it works. You still pay nothing until it&rsquo;s saving your team 5 hours a week.</li>
            <li><b>What we ask.</b> We measure before and after, and you let us share the result, with your name or without it. Your choice.</li>
            <li><b>What stays the same.</b> <span data-zar="2950">R2,950</span> a month once you keep it, a person checks every reply, and you own your data.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="founding__left"><b data-f-left>5</b> of <span data-f-total2>5</span> places left<span data-f-ends></span>. A place is taken when a client decides to keep it.</p>
          <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="https://calendar.app.google/58FYamh1ahXB4khM9" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track="cta-founding-book">Book a free 30-minute call</a></div>
          <p class="tiny muted founding__small">For businesses that qualify (20+ customer emails a day). One place per business, not combined with other discounts.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- what's included -->
    <section class="section" id="included" aria-labelledby="inclTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">What the monthly fee covers</span>
          <h2 id="inclTitle">One price. Nothing extra to work out.</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="ia-incl reveal">
          <li><b>AI usage included</b><span>Up to 1,500 emails a month. Busier than that? We&rsquo;ll tell you before it costs more.</span></li>
          <li><b>Kept up to date</b><span>New prices, a new policy, a new service: send it and we update it.</span></li>
          <li><b>Checked every month</b><span>We review a sample of drafts for accuracy and fix anything that drifts.</span></li>
          <li><b>Time saved, reported</b><span>A short report each month: emails handled and hours given back.</span></li>
          <li><b>A reply by the next business day</b><span>WhatsApp or email, from the person who built it.</span></li>
          <li><b>Month to month after 3 months</b><span>The 3 months start once you keep it. After that, stop any time with a month&rsquo;s notice. Your data stays yours.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--tint" id="faq" aria-labelledby="iaFaqTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
          <h2 id="iaFaqTitle">Questions.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq reveal">
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Does it send emails by itself?</summary><p>No. It writes the reply on your page; a person checks it, copies it into your email and presses send. Anything it isn&rsquo;t sure of is marked for you to fill in.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What if it gets something wrong?</summary><p>Then the person checking it fixes it before it goes out, and tells us, and we correct it so it doesn&rsquo;t happen again. We also review a sample every month.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Which email does it work with?</summary><p>Any of them: Gmail, Outlook or whatever you use, because you paste the email into your page. On Microsoft 365 we can also have the drafts waiting in your inbox, with no pasting at all.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Will it sound like us?</summary><p>Yes. We set it up from your own past replies, your tone and your sign-off, and it answers in the language the customer wrote in, including Afrikaans.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What happens to our data?</summary><p>It&rsquo;s used only to draft your replies, under POPIA. We don&rsquo;t keep the emails you paste, only a one-line note of what each was about. If you don&rsquo;t keep it, we switch your page off and delete it. <a class="inline-link" href="privacy">Privacy</a></p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>When do we pay?</summary><p>Only at the end. We set it up and your team uses it for two weeks at no cost. If it&rsquo;s saving your team at least 5 hours a week, measured the way we agreed on day one, you pay the <span data-zar="9500">R9,500</span> setup and the <span data-zar="2950">R2,950</span> monthly plan starts. If it isn&rsquo;t, you pay nothing. It needs the access and information we agreed on day one.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>We get fewer than 20 emails a day. Is it worth it?</summary><p>Probably not yet, and we&rsquo;ll say so. A few saved replies or a shared template might do the job. If your volume grows, we can look again.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta" aria-labelledby="ctaTitle">
      <div class="container cta__inner reveal">
        <h2 id="ctaTitle">See if your inbox qualifies.</h2>
        <p>A free 30-minute call. We look at your emails with you and tell you honestly whether it&rsquo;s worth it.</p>
        <div class="btn-row btn-row--center">
          <a class="btn btn--light btn--large" href="https://calendar.app.google/58FYamh1ahXB4khM9" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track="cta-inbox-book">Book a free 30-minute call</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="callwhat" aria-label="What happens on the free call"><li>You tell us about the work</li><li>We say honestly if AI fits</li><li>No slides, no pitch</li><li>You leave with a rough price, or an honest &ldquo;not worth it&rdquo;</li></ul>
        <p class="cta__alt">Prefer to write? <button type="button" class="inline-link" data-review-open>Tell us in a few lines</button></p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <script src="try-email.js" defer></script>
